WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.910
- I've seen your request,
I've read your comments

00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:05.380
so here we go, intermittent fasting.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:06.690
- I am dying to talk to you about this.

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.080
- I eat for eight hours,
and I fast for 16.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:10.450
- I can feel the difference.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.220
- Before we get into the pros and cons,

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:13.490
and if you should do it,

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:16.340
let's talk about what
intermittent fasting actually is.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:19.320
Human fasting is not a
new concept by any means.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:21.820
Humans have been doing it for a millennia.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.610
Intermittent fasting is just a rebranding

00:00:24.610 --> 00:00:26.790
of something that we
have already been doing.

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:30.710
Our bodies enter a fasting
state every time we're asleep.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.820
Some people do intermittent
fasting and not even know it.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.340
I mean, there's plenty of times where I

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.258
had a stressful rotation
in medical school,

00:00:37.258 --> 00:00:39.400
or a difficult job in the hospital,

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.190
where I didn't have time to eat breakfast.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.370
That's a form of intermittent fasting

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.890
and our bodies are totally
capable of handling this.

00:00:45.890 --> 00:00:47.150
I know what you're thinking.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.535
I don't want to starve
myself for health benefits.

00:00:49.535 --> 00:00:51.745
Intermittent fasting is not starving.

00:00:51.745 --> 00:00:55.033
When you are fasting, your
body is using stored nutrients

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.109
and stored energy forms in order

00:00:57.109 --> 00:00:59.370
to make your body continue to function.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:00.203
When you're starving,

00:01:00.203 --> 00:01:02.460
you've run out of those energy sources

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:04.777
and are breaking down
vital tissues like organs

00:01:04.777 --> 00:01:06.260
to get that same energy.

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:09.020
There are many different
ways to go about going

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:12.010
on one of these diets and that
not only makes it confusing

00:01:12.010 --> 00:01:14.400
for you, but that also
makes it very difficult

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.288
to do research on it to find
out how effective it truly is

00:01:17.288 --> 00:01:19.661
because if there are
multiple ways to do it,

00:01:19.661 --> 00:01:22.500
we have to be able to test
each one of those ways.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.700
The 16/8 diet which is not eating

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.210
during 16 hours of the day.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.863
Alternate day fasting
where you eat one day,

00:01:28.863 --> 00:01:30.170
fast the other day.

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:33.170
5:2 where two days of the
week that you're fasting.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:35.570
There's no hard and fast rule saying

00:01:35.570 --> 00:01:37.290
that this is the correct way of doing it.

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:41.180
You may be wondering how
is IF beneficial to me?

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:43.510
There's been a lot of
proposed health benefits,

00:01:43.510 --> 00:01:46.013
many of them have been
proven within animal studies

00:01:46.013 --> 00:01:48.410
or lab models which is not the same thing

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:49.904
as being proven in a human model.

00:01:49.904 --> 00:01:52.008
But they are very promising.

00:01:52.008 --> 00:01:55.223
Now, those benefits include
increased mental sharpness,

00:01:55.223 --> 00:01:58.729
a favorable hormonal profile, weight loss,

00:01:58.729 --> 00:02:01.320
decreases of inflammation within the body,

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:03.660
decreases of certain
diseases within the body.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:05.990
How can IF help you lose weight?

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:07.730
You have an increase in growth hormone,

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:09.810
a decrease in insulin, and that alone

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:10.807
will help you lose weight.

00:02:10.807 --> 00:02:13.228
Next, because you're skipping meals

00:02:13.228 --> 00:02:15.405
or you're even going days
without eating meals,

00:02:15.405 --> 00:02:18.009
it is very likely that when
you look throughout the week,

00:02:18.009 --> 00:02:20.070
you'll be eating fewer calories.

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.750
Our thinking is that during
eight hours you'll eat less

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.280
than you would if you were
eating during 16 hours.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:27.570
Let's talk about these
other health benefits.

00:02:27.570 --> 00:02:30.270
We know that chronic stress
is not good for the body.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:33.050
The body is just not meant to
be chronically stressed out.

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.635
It's not meant to have a high heart rate,

00:02:34.635 --> 00:02:36.210
high blood pressure.

00:02:36.210 --> 00:02:38.247
Intermittent fasting is really a form

00:02:38.247 --> 00:02:41.860
acute, short-term, mild stress.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.091
This time of acute, short-term stress

00:02:44.091 --> 00:02:46.320
is really good for the body.

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.420
What can we use as a metaphor here?

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.160
Let's take exercise.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:53.329
Exercise is a form of acute, mild stress.

00:02:53.329 --> 00:02:55.880
What happens after exercise?

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.560
We have benefits for the brain,

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:58.811
we have benefits for weight loss,

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:01.570
we have benefits for disease prevention.

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:03.610
Now similarly, when you stress your body

00:03:03.610 --> 00:03:05.845
through intermittent fasting,
there are some benefits.

00:03:05.845 --> 00:03:09.377
More autophagy, which is the
removal of cellular waste,

00:03:09.377 --> 00:03:12.500
more production of neurotropic factors,

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:13.960
which protect your brain.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.970
And a favorable hormonal profile

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:19.300
with increases in human growth
hormone and norepinephrine.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.620
Let's talk about some of
the shortcoming of IF.

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:23.812
Primarily, there's not enough guidance

00:03:23.812 --> 00:03:25.920
of what you should eat.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.490
We don't know how many calories,

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:29.708
we don't know what foods
to eat on the days or times

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:31.070
that you actually are eating.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:33.982
Second, we don't know
which form of IF is best.

00:03:33.982 --> 00:03:37.167
Third, there are some side
effects when you are fasting

00:03:37.167 --> 00:03:41.841
that people do experience:
headaches, mental fog, heartburn,

00:03:41.841 --> 00:03:44.680
these things do exist,
it's not totally benign.

00:03:44.680 --> 00:03:47.180
Four, we don't know the consequences

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:50.410
of following an intermittent
fasting diet long term.

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:52.300
Most, if not all, of these studies

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.900
are done on the short term.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:56.340
If you are eating a very unhealthy diet

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:59.069
and then make a change you're
definitely gonna see a benefit

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:02.990
But now does this benefit
still hold up one, two, three,

00:04:02.990 --> 00:04:04.630
10 years down the line?

00:04:04.630 --> 00:04:07.010
We don't know that yet
when it comes to IF.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:09.840
And five, it's not easy for everybody

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:12.380
to fight off those
cravings on fasting days.

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.817
All righty, my final take on IF,

00:04:14.817 --> 00:04:16.577
I think it is a great concept

00:04:16.577 --> 00:04:19.590
with some really promising
medical research behind it.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.748
I think that if you can skip a meal,

00:04:21.748 --> 00:04:23.870
you can skip a breakfast here and there,

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:25.255
you're gonna see some benefits.

00:04:25.255 --> 00:04:29.190
Does that mean you should
go on this very rigid diet

00:04:29.190 --> 00:04:32.280
where you're doing the five
and two or 16 and eight?

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.471
I don't think we should
quite make this a religious,

00:04:34.471 --> 00:04:36.605
rigorous part of our everyday life

00:04:36.605 --> 00:04:39.520
because we don't know the
long term consequences of it.

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:41.621
But in a society that
is prone to overeating,

00:04:41.621 --> 00:04:46.160
a fasting day won't hurt
and will probably help.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:48.596
As always, stay happy and healthy.

00:04:48.596 --> 00:04:51.300
So here we go, intermittent fasting:

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:53.724
kind of ate the word intermittent,
it was like borderline.

00:04:53.724 --> 00:04:56.671
Our bodies have adapted to
this sort of fasting period

00:04:56.671 --> 00:05:00.055
because of throughout the millennia, blah,

00:05:00.055 --> 00:05:01.340
(growling)

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:02.640
May people are doing this already

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:03.858
and not not...

00:05:03.858 --> 00:05:07.014
Our bodies are totally
capable and have adapted

00:05:07.014 --> 00:05:10.537
to not being filled with
food 24 hours of the day.

00:05:10.537 --> 00:05:11.370
(laughing)

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:12.203
Why are you laughing?

00:05:12.203 --> 00:05:13.630
Creating more mitochondria

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:16.921
which is the energy making
machinery of the cell.

00:05:16.921 --> 00:05:18.380
Energy making?

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:21.843
Which is the energy
center of the sill, sill?

00:05:21.843 --> 00:05:23.526
(exhales)

00:05:23.526 --> 00:05:25.393
(laughing)

00:05:25.393 --> 00:05:28.143
